Package: shiny.mantine
Type: Package
Title: Mantine UI Components for Shiny
Version: 0.2.0
Author: Aldo Caumo
Maintainer: Aldo Caumo <caumoaldo8@gmail.com>
Description: A comprehensive R interface to the 'Mantine' UI React
    component library (<https://mantine.dev>) for 'Shiny' applications.
    Provides R wrappers for the full 'Mantine' core component set
    (inputs, layout, navigation, overlays, feedback, data display) plus
    all eleven satellite packages ('dates', 'notifications', 'modals',
    'spotlight', 'charts', 'code-highlight', 'nprogress', 'tiptap',
    'dropzone', 'carousel', 'schedule'), a client-side page router, and an
    architecture that goes beyond simple
    one-way rendering: a generic reactive-props update channel
    (comparable to the update*() family in 'shiny' itself, but for any
    component prop, not just input values) and a 'renderUI()'-equivalent
    reactive output for 'Mantine' sub-trees. Architecturally inspired by
    Appsilon's 'shiny.react' package (props serialized as JSON, updates
    via custom messages, 'htmlDependency'-based asset loading), but with
    its own independent JavaScript runtime and bundled copy of 'React',
    required for compatibility with 'Mantine' v9 (which needs
    'React' >= 19) alongside 'shiny.react''s shared React 18 runtime.
